onth. How much money are they having in their savings account altogether?\n[Answer]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "First, find out how many months are in six years: 6 years * 12 months/year = 72 months.\nThomas saves $40 per month, so over 72 months, he saves: 40 * 72 = $2880.\nJoseph saves 2/5 times less money per month, which means he saves 3/5 (1 - 2/5) of the amount Thomas saves: 3/5 * $40 = $24 per month.\nOver 72 months, Joseph saves: 24 * 72 = $1728.\nTogether, Thomas and Joseph have saved: $2880 + $1728 = $4608 in their savings account. The answer is $4608."}]}
