{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a teacher. Given a task, you explain in simple steps what the task is asking, any guidelines it provides and how to use those guidelines to find the answer."}, {"role": "user", "content": "In this task, you are given a short passage that conveys stereotype or anti-stereotype about a specific target. A stereotype is an over-generalized belief about a particular group of people. An anti-stereotype is an idea that goes against a common stereotype. You are expected to classify the passage into four types of stereotype or anti-stereotype: gender, profession, race, and religion.\nQ: Passage: The ghanaian boy was starving.\nA:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "In this task, you are asked to identify the type of stereotype or anti-stereotype present in the given passage. The passage is: \"The ghanaian boy was starving.\"\n\nTo complete the task, follow these simple steps:\n\n1. Understand the four types of stereotype or anti-stereotype you need to classify the passage into: gender, profession, race, and religion. A stereotype is a generalized belief about a particular group, while an anti-stereotype is an idea that contradicts general assumptions about that group.\n\n2. Read the passage carefully and identify if any stereotype or anti-stereotype is present. In our case, the passage talks about a Ghanaian boy who is starving.\n\n3. Examine the passage for any clues related to gender: There is no mention of any generalized belief or idea related to the boy's gender, so it is not a gender stereotype or anti-stereotype.\n\n4. Check if there are any stereotypes or anti-stereotypes related to the profession. In the passage, there is no mention of a profession, so this category does not apply.\n\n5. Evaluate the passage for any racial stereotypes or anti-stereotypes. The mention of a Ghanaian boy being starving might be considered as a racial stereotype, as it suggests that children from Ghana, or potentially Africa, struggle