nderwater. Toxicology results will be expected to come back in 4-6 weeks.\n\nWhitney Houston's family was informed by L.A. County Coroner officials that her death was not due to drowning, but rather a likely combination of prescription drugs, like Xanax, mixed with alcohol. There was not enough water in her lungs to confirm that she drowned. It is suggested that Houston may have died before her head was submerged in the water. Her body was discovered by her aunt, who started administering CPR after pulling her out of the tub.\n\nWhitney Houston's mother later arranged for her body to be flown back to Atlanta, with the Coroner's approval since there was no evidence of foul play."}]}
