sted Tasmanian Wilderness World Heritage Area, and visiting the wildlife-rich Bruny Island.\n\nIn summary, Hobart is the capital city of Tasmania, an island state that forms part of the Commonwealth of Australia. With its rich history, thriving arts and culture, and access to breathtaking natural landscapes, Hobart is an attractive destination for tourists and residents alike."}]}
