larWinds Event Log Consolidator, and Log Parser Lizard.\n\n3. Convert the EVTX file to a different format: If you want to view the contents of the EVTX file in a more human-readable format, you can use a tool like Log Parser Studio from Microsoft or the aforementioned Log Parser Lizard to convert the file into CSV, XML, or HTML format. You can then open the converted file using a spreadsheet application like Microsoft Excel or a text editor that supports the chosen format.\n\nIn summary, EVTX files are event log files used by the Windows operating system, and you can open them using built-in tools like the Windows Event Viewer or third-party event log viewers. Understanding the nature of the EVTX file extension helps you take the necessary steps to view and analyze the event logs stored within these files, which can be invaluable for troubleshooting and monitoring system performance."}]}
