ween the Palestinians and the Israelis. And I think this was a sensitive area in which the president didn't want to be involved.\" \n Answer: he refuses to provide advice for Obama's administration\nSolution:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "In this task, you are given an article about Former President Jimmy Carter's belief that the U.S central intelligence agency is spying on him and his decision to give up email. Your task is to generate a fill-in-the-blank question based on this article for the answer \"he refuses to provide advice for Obama's administration\". \n\nSteps:\n\n1. Read the article carefully and understand the main points discussed.\n2. Identify any guidelines or rules given in the detailed instructions, such as the blanks being at the end of the question and allowing for multiple words or phrases.\n3. Focus on the part of the article which talks about why Jimmy Carter does not provide advice for Obama's administration. In this case, it's the part where Carter says, \"I think the problem was that in dealing with the issue of peace between Israel and Egypt, the Carter Center took a very strong and public position of equal treatment between the Palestinians and the Israelis. And I think this was a sensitive area in which the president didn't want to be involved.\"\n4. Use this information to generate a fill-in-the-blank question related to the answer given.\n\nExample fill-in-the-blank question:\n\nFormer President Jimmy Carter does not provide advice for Obama's administration because of the Carter Center's position on peace between Israel and Egypt and the president's reluctance to be involved in this sensitive area. Therefore, he _______________."}]}
