ugh to Deveraux. What they did not foresee however is that John also holds the government responsible for his pain, whether or not Deveraux killed his family or not: if he did then the government set him up to it in order to make him want to kill Deveraux. It's the same to John. After Deveraux let himself be killed, John is now the respected leader of the other universal soldiers. The story gets in a stream acceleration in the end, because apparently they went and got the last container that had to be sent \"upstream\" which contained the last equipment needed to clone people. When John meets with the FBI agent again he is not alone. The agent boosts about his achievement (by giving John false memories) but John kills him... and replaces the agent with a clone. From there we can guess what kind of fight is going to follow, but I suppose that will indeed be part of a future movie.\nOutput:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Question: What is the main objective of implanting false memories in John?\nAnswer: To make John think he has free will and make him want to hunt down and kill Deveraux.\n\nQuestion: Why is Deveraux wanted by the government?\nAnswer: Because he's running an underground organisation that frees clones like John from the government, gives them the truth, and removes their false memories.\n\nQuestion: What did the previous John do after being freed by Deveraux?\nAnswer: He worked for Deveraux for a while, then left him because he felt he was now the slave of Deveraux instead of the government.\n\nQuestion: Who hunts down John and eventually gets killed by him?\nAnswer: Magnus, played by Andrei Arlovski.\n\nQuestion: What does John decide to do when offered to have his false memories removed?\nAnswer: He freaks out and goes on a killing spree, holding onto his memories as real.\n\nQuestion: At the end of the story, who becomes the respected leader of the other universal soldiers?\nAnswer: John.\n\nQuestion: What does John do to the FBI agent at the end of the story?\nAnswer: He kills him and replaces him with a clone."}]}
