eally angry and I texted my dad everything and sent him pictures of everything. I was also being impulsive and messaged my mom and told her what I found and how it was stupid of her to waste all of my dad’s time to be with her if she’s in an unhappy relationship. So my mom got home and went apeshit on me and basically was telling me how that’s just how people talk and that my dad and her were fine before I got in the way and started telling him this stuff. So for awhile after that I’ve kept trying to tell my dad to just get a divorce because he’s always complaining about my mom, and I hate that they bring me into their problems and complain about each other to me as it affects me too.  But my dad keeps telling me once he has a stable job he’ll leave (my mom is the breadwinner in my family) and I was recently told my mom would have gotten a divorce with my dad if she wasn’t at risk to lose things that she’s worked hard for. \n\nEvery time I intersect one of their arguments it’s always my mom bringing up stupid little things to my dad and I tend to be very blunt and harsh towards her because what she’s screaming to my dad about is not important. For example, my dad went out for lunch today with his brother (she also went out for lunch yesterday with a friend) and my mom created this huge deal out of it and turned it into she does everything and he does nothing. Which could be farther from the truth, my whole life my dad has supported my brother always trying to make us happy. So every single time my mom brings up a small thing and creates it into an argument I always tell her that she does the exact same thing and she’s being extremely hypocritical for screaming at him for doing something she did yesterday. Every time I tell her how hypocritical and immature she’s being she starts turning it around on me telling me that I’m ungrateful, unappreciative, entitled and etc. Now I feel like I’m always being bitchy to my mom which I hate doing but every time I try to have a 