om the Ottoman Empire. Although the Orlov Revolt itself was ultimately unsuccessful and was brutally suppressed by the Ottomans, it planted the seeds for future Greek struggle for independence, which eventually materialized with the outbreak of the Greek War of Independence in 1821.\n\nIn summary, the Orlov Revolt was instigated by Russia for its own strategic interests, primarily to weaken and break up the Ottoman Empire so that it could expand its influence and territories in the region. However, the revolt also had an impact on the Greek nation, as it nurtured Greek nationalist sentiments and contributed to their struggle for independence from the Ottoman Empire."}]}
