{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI assistant. User will you give you a task. Your goal is to complete the task as faithfully as you can. While performing the task think step-by-step and justify your steps."}, {"role": "user", "content": "According to the 2011 census of India, the total population of Karnataka was 61,095,297 of which 30,966,657 (50.7%) were male and 30,128,640 (49.3%) were female, or 1000 males for every 973 females. This represents a 15.60% increase over the population in 2001. The population density was 319 per km2 and 38.67% of the people lived in urban areas. The literacy rate was 75.36% with 82.47% of males and 68.08% of females being literate. 84.00% of the population were Hindu, 12.92% were Muslim, 1.87% were Christian, 0.72% were Jains, 0.16% were Buddhist, 0.05% were Sikh and 0.02% were belonging to other religions and 0.27% of the population did not state their religion.\n\nBased on the above article, answer a question. How many females are not literate?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To find out how many females are not literate, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the total number of females in Karnataka.\n2. Calculate the number of literate females using the given literacy rate.\n3. Subtract the number of literate females from the total number of females to find the number of females who are not literate.\n\nStep 1: Total number of females in Karnataka\nFrom the information provided, the total number of females in Karnataka in 2011 was 30,128,640.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the number of literate females\nThe female literacy rate in 2011 was 68.08%. Therefore, the number of literate females can be calculated as follows:\nLiterate females = Total females × Female literacy rate\nLiterate females = 30,128,640 × 0.6808\nLiterate females ≈ 20,499,554\n\nStep 3: Calculate the number of females who are not literate\nNow, we subtract the number of literate females from the total number of females:\nNon-literate females = Total females - Literate females\nNon-literate females = 30,128,640 - 20,499,554\nNon-literate females ≈ 9,629,086\n\nTherefore, about 9,629,086 females in Karnataka were not literate according to the 2011 census."}]}
