maining. The remaining 2 shirts cost 20 * 2 = 40 dollars in total. The five shirts cost 45 + 40 = 85 dollars.\nThe answer: 85\nReverse engineering the question: Five shirts are bought. Of the 5 shirts, there are 3 shirts that cost $15 each. The remaining shirts are $20 each. What is the cost, in dollars, of all 5 shirts?\n\nReasoning and answer: They sold in the morning and afternoon for a total of 29 + 17 = 46 bags. Each bag weighs 7kg so 46 bags weigh 46 * 7kg = 322kg.\nThe answer: 322\nWhat was the question?\nQuestion: A shop sold 29 bags of potatoes in the morning. In the afternoon, the shop sold 17 bags of potatoes. If each bag of potatoes weighs 7kg, how many kilograms of potatoes did the shop sell for the whole day?\n\nReasoning and answer: After keeping 15 cards, Rick had 130 cards - 15 cards = 115 cards left. The total number of cards given by Rick to his 8 friends was 8 friends x 12 cards / friend = 96 cards. There were 2 sisters x 3 cards / sister = 6 cards given to Rick's sisters. So, there were 96 cards + 6 cards = 102 cards left after Rick gave Miguel some cards. Therefore, 115 cards - 102 cards = 13 cards were given to Miguel.\nThe answer: 13\nWhat was the question?\nQuestion:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Rick had 130 trading cards. He decided to keep 15 cards for himself and distributed the remaining cards among his friends and sisters. He gave each of his 8 friends 12 cards and each of his 2 sisters 3 cards. How many cards did Rick give to his friend Miguel?"}]}
