e, rather than to attach themselves to the nearest Heavy. The announcement of \"I am charged!\" can be heard by nearby enemies. If you wish to cover up this tell-tale signal so they are less likely to be prepared for it, you can call for a Medic (or any other vocal command) just as the meter reaches 100%, and it will override the passive \"I am charged!\" announcement.\n\nSummary:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "A Medic in the game has three main tools: a Syringe Gun for shooting from a distance, a Medi-Gun for healing teammates, and a Bonesaw for close fighting. The Medic can unlock more weapons by finishing achievements. You should use the Bonesaw only when you're really close to an enemy, and it's better to heal your teammates and let them fight instead. The Syringe Gun shoots needles that go a little to the right and down, so you need to aim up and left to hit enemies far away. It's good for slowing down enemies as well. \n\nThe Medi-Gun can heal friends from far away, making them feel better and even stronger than usual. This helps the team because your friends can fight better and you can help them by looking out for sneaky enemies. When you heal a lot, you can use a special power called ÜberCharge that makes you and your friend invincible for a short time. But, you can't win the game while using it, so use it to help your friends in tough fights. Remember to heal all your friends, not just the big strong ones, to be a good Medic and keep the team strong and healthy."}]}
